WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.239
“Insights”

2
00:00:01.239 --> 00:00:05.569
calculates portfolio, production and pipeline from your own data:

3
00:00:05.756 --> 00:00:10.782
the last thirty days, calls, meetings, new clients and cases issued,

4
00:00:10.969 --> 00:00:16.390
the portfolio by branch, the top insurers and the pipeline by stage.

5
00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:22.075
In “Production”, every premium change is credited exactly once:

6
00:00:22.447 --> 00:00:27.810
new business, increases, decreases, renewals and reversals.

7
00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:29.781
The “Business center”

8
00:00:29.781 --> 00:00:33.007
keeps targets, production, activity and service separate.

9
00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:35.609
The goals you set during set-up become pace

10
00:00:35.609 --> 00:00:38.023
bars that show where you should be today.

11
00:00:39.123 --> 00:00:40.307
The “Client list”

12
00:00:40.307 --> 00:00:42.409
shows every client, since when they have

13
00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:44.474
been a client and where they came from.

14
00:00:45.032 --> 00:00:47.435
You print it on A4 with your own branding,

15
00:00:47.494 --> 00:00:50.604
or export it as CSV for Excel.

16
00:00:51.704 --> 00:00:53.955
Everything is calculated from your own data.

17
00:00:54.142 --> 00:00:57.102
So the more complete your records, the truer the picture:

18
00:00:57.404 --> 00:00:58.635
in the “Client list”

19
00:00:58.635 --> 00:01:01.188
you fill in missing sources and dates.

20
00:01:02.288 --> 00:01:03.367
In the next lesson:

21
00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:06.014
backups and the security of your data.
